  ...READ('MK5-r', 'Reading, A pitch for Green Leaf Cold Brew',
    `Good afternoon, and thank you for meeting us. My name is Linh, and I work in marketing at Green Leaf Tea.\n\nHo Chi Minh City is hot all year, and many young office workers want a cold drink that is healthy and quick. Today I would like to introduce Green Leaf Cold Brew, our new bottled tea.\n\nFirst, the product. We brew Da Lat green tea slowly in cold water for twelve hours, so it is smoother and less bitter than hot-brewed tea. It also has much less sugar than most bottled teas: only four grams per bottle.\n\nSecond, price and place. A 330 ml bottle costs 25,000 VND. That is a little more expensive than ordinary bottled tea, but it is much cheaper than a cup of tea from a cafe. We would like to sell it in your forty Sao Mai Mart stores, next to the fresh juice.\n\nFinally, promotion. In June we will give free tastings in twenty of your stores, and we will post short videos on TikTok every week.\n\nOur first customers say it is the most refreshing tea they have ever tried. Shall we start with a trial order of 2,000 bottles?`, [
      M('MK5', 'Main idea', 'What is the main purpose of Linh\'s pitch?',
        ['To explain how to brew tea at home', 'To compare Sao Mai Mart with other supermarkets', 'To persuade a supermarket to sell a new bottled tea', 'To announce a new Green Leaf Tea shop'], 2,
        'Linh introduces the cold brew and ends with "Shall we start with a trial order of 2,000 bottles?" She wants the supermarket to sell it.'),
      M('MK5', 'Detail', 'How long does Green Leaf Tea brew the cold brew?',
        ['Four hours', 'Twelve hours', 'Twenty hours', 'Two days'], 1,
        '"We brew Da Lat green tea slowly in cold water for twelve hours." Four is the number of grams of sugar.'),
      M('MK5', 'Vocabulary in context', 'The cold brew is "smoother" than hot-brewed tea. What does "smoother" mean here?',
        ['colder and better in summer', 'stronger and more bitter', 'more expensive to make', 'softer and easier to drink'], 3,
        'A smooth drink is soft in the mouth; the text links it with "less bitter".'),
    ]),
  ...LISTEN('MK5-l', 'Listening, Choosing a gift box for Tet',
    `Okay, everyone, let's look at the three gift box designs for Tet. Box A is red and gold, with four kinds of tea. It's the biggest box, but it's also the most expensive: five hundred and fifty thousand dong. Box B is smaller and lighter, with two teas and some dried strawberries from Da Lat. It costs three hundred and twenty thousand dong. Box C is the cheapest, only two hundred thousand, but honestly, the design is less attractive than the other two. Last year, most of our customers were companies buying gifts for their staff, and they wanted something good, but not too expensive. So I think Box B is the best choice for us. Linh, could you ask Mr Tran how quickly his farm can send the tea? We need an answer by Thursday.`, [
      M('MK5', 'Gist', 'What is the meeting mainly about?',
        ['Opening a new shop for Tet', 'Choosing a gift box design for Tet', 'Finding a new tea supplier', 'Planning a staff party'], 1,
        'The speaker compares "the three gift box designs for Tet" and chooses one.'),
      M('MK5', 'Specific information', 'How much does Box B cost?',
        ['550,000 VND', '200,000 VND', '320,000 VND', '230,000 VND'], 2,
        '"It costs three hundred and twenty thousand dong." 550,000 is Box A and 200,000 is Box C.'),
      M('MK5', 'Speaker\'s opinion', 'Which box does the speaker think is best, and why?',
        ['Box B, because company buyers want good quality at a fair price', 'Box B, because it is the lightest box and the easiest to deliver', 'Box A, because company buyers want the biggest box at Tet', 'Box C, because company buyers want the lowest price'], 0,
        '"They wanted something good, but not too expensive. So I think Box B is the best choice for us." She says Box B is lighter, but that is not her reason.'),
    ]),
  ...SPEAK('MK5', 'Speaking, Pitch a product in one minute',
    'You are a sales assistant at Green Leaf Tea. Mr Phuc, a shop owner in District 7, is thinking of selling your mango tea biscuits. Pitch them for about 1 minute.\nNotes: made with Da Lat green tea and real mango; lighter and less sweet than normal biscuits; the most popular snack with students in our shops; 35,000 VND for a pack of 8 (imported biscuits: about 45,000 VND); delivery every Monday; minimum order 20 packs.\n• Open with a hook and introduce the product.\n• Make at least two comparisons and one superlative.\n• Give the price and delivery, and end with a clear request.\nUse: lighter / less sweet / cheaper than, the most popular, Why don\'t you…?',
    `Good morning, Mr Phuc. Do your customers want a healthy snack with their tea? Let me introduce our mango tea biscuits from Green Leaf Tea. They are made with Da Lat green tea and real mango, so they are lighter and less sweet than normal biscuits. In our own shops, they are the most popular snack with students. A pack of eight costs 35,000 VND, which is cheaper than most imported biscuits. We deliver every Monday, and the smallest order is only twenty packs. Why don't you try one box this month? If your customers don't like them, we will take them back.`,
    ['Language: uses comparatives (-er than, less … than) and superlatives (the most …) accurately, at least three times, and a polite request (Why don\'t you…? / Would you like to…?)', 'Task: includes the hook, the product, the price, the delivery and a clear request from the notes', 'Delivery: clear, steady pace, understandable pronunciation']),
  ...WRITE('MK5', 'Writing, A product pitch email',
    'You are Linh, marketing assistant at Green Leaf Tea. Write an email of about 120 words to Ms Tran Thi Hoa, the owner of Hoa Coffee, a group of cafes near the universities in Thu Duc. Purpose: persuade her to sell Green Leaf oolong tea in her cafes.\nNotes: grown on a family farm in Bao Loc; lighter than coffee and less caffeine, so good for students who study late; the most popular hot tea in our shops; 500-gram bag = 220,000 VND, about 120 cups (cheaper per cup than milk tea); next step: free tasting next week, then a trial order of ten bags.\n• Introduce the product and say why it suits students.\n• Compare it with other drinks.\n• Give the price and suggest a next step.\nUse: lighter than, less … than, cheaper than, the most popular; Would you like us to…?',
    `Dear Ms Hoa,\n\nI am writing to introduce Green Leaf oolong tea, grown on a family farm in Bao Loc.\n\nMany students in Thu Duc study late and want a drink that keeps them awake. Our oolong is lighter than coffee and has less caffeine, so students can enjoy it in the evening and still sleep well. It is also the most popular hot tea in our own shops.\n\nA 500-gram bag costs 220,000 VND and makes about 120 cups, so it is cheaper per cup than most milk tea.\n\nWould you like us to hold a free tasting in one of your cafes next week? After that, you could try a small order of ten bags.\n\nI look forward to hearing from you.\n\nBest regards,\nLinh\nGreen Leaf Tea`,
    ['Language: uses comparatives (-er than, less … than) and at least one superlative accurately, with so / because to give reasons', 'Task: includes the product, why it suits students, the price and the next step from the notes', 'Organisation: email opening with purpose, one paragraph per point, polite request and closing'], 120),

